<nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" style="max-width:1180px;margin:0 auto;padding:14px 24px;">
  <ol style="list-style:none;padding:0;margin:0;display:flex;gap:8px;font-size:13px;color:#7A8490;">
    <li><a href="/" style="color:#8F5D0C;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600;">Home</a></li>
    <li>/</li>
    <li style="color:#16202E;">About</li>
  </ol>
</nav>
<section style="background:linear-gradient(150deg,#101826 0%,#16202E 55%,#1B2A3C 100%);padding:76px 24px 84px;">
  <div style="max-width:1180px;margin:0 auto;">
    <span class="kicker-dark">About Us</span>
    <h1 style="font-family:'Plus Jakarta Sans',sans-serif;font-weight:800;color:#fff;line-height:1.1;letter-spacing:-1px;font-size:clamp(32px,4.2vw,48px);max-width:820px;margin:0 0 18px;">About Greeley Solar Reset</h1>
    <p style="font-size:17px;line-height:1.7;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.72);max-width:620px;margin:0 0 30px;">We take solar panels off, protect them while your roofer works, and put them back exactly where they belong. That's the whole job, and we do it well.</p>
    <div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:16px;">
      <a href="/#contact" class="btn-green">Get a Free Estimate</a>
      <a href="tel:+19702863417" class="btn-outline-white"><svg width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 16.92v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.18 2 19.79 19.79 0 0 1-8.63-3.07A19.5 19.5 0 0 1 4.5 12 19.79 19.79 0 0 1 1.1 3.18a2 2 0 0 1 2-2.18h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.72c.127.96.361 1.903.7 2.81a2 2 0 0 1-.45 2.11L7.91 8.27a16 16 0 0 0 7.82 7.82l1.27-1.27a2 2 0 0 1 2.11-.45c.907.339 1.85.573 2.81.7A2 2 0 0 1 22 16.92z"/></svg> (970) 286-3417</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
<section style="padding:80px 24px 8px;background:#fff;"><div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;">
    <div class="rich"><p>Greeley Solar Reset started with a problem we kept seeing all over Northern Colorado. A hailstorm rolls through, a homeowner gets a new roof approved, and then the roofer says the same thing every roofer says: we don't touch solar panels. Suddenly the whole project stalls while everyone figures out who handles the array.</p><p>So that's what we do. <a href="/solar-detach-reset-greeley/">Solar detach and reset</a> is our only trade, not a side service bolted onto something else. We remove your panels, label and store them safely, coordinate with your roofing crew, and reinstall everything once the new roof is on. We test the system before we leave so you know it's producing like it should.</p><p>Because most of our work comes out of hail season, we've learned how insurance claims actually move around here. We know what adjusters look for, how detach and reset shows up in a scope, and when a supplement makes sense. We're not adjusters and we won't pretend to be, but we document our work thoroughly and we'll walk you through <a href="/solar-panel-removal-reinstall-cost/">what the work really costs</a> so nothing in your claim is a guess.</p><p>We're based in Greeley and we work across Weld and Larimer counties, from Evans and Eaton up through Windsor and down to Firestone and Fort Lupton. Every estimate is free and in writing, we're licensed and insured, and our <a href="/emergency-solar-service-greeley/">emergency line</a> answers around the clock when a storm tears something loose.</p></div>
  </div></section>
<section class="section-pad bg-light"><div class="container">
    <div style="max-width:820px;margin:0 0 48px;">
    <span class="kicker">How We Work</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(24px,3vw,32px);margin:0 0 14px;">What You Can Expect</h2>
  </div>
    <div class="gsr-grid-2">
      <div class="card" style="padding:30px 28px;">
        <div style="margin-bottom:16px;"><span style="flex-shrink:0;display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;width:48px;height:48px;border-radius:50%;background:#FBF2DF;"><svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#8F5D0C" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 11.08V12a10 10 0 1 1-5.93-9.14"/><polyline points="22 4 12 14.01 9 11.01"/></svg></span></div>
        <h3 style="font-size:18px;font-weight:800;margin:0 0 8px;">Written estimates, no surprises</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#4A5560;margin:0;">You get a free written estimate before we touch a panel. The number you approve is the number you pay unless the scope genuinely changes, and if it does, we explain why first.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card" style="padding:30px 28px;">
        <div style="margin-bottom:16px;"><span style="flex-shrink:0;display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;width:48px;height:48px;border-radius:50%;background:#FBF2DF;"><svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#8F5D0C" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 11.08V12a10 10 0 1 1-5.93-9.14"/><polyline points="22 4 12 14.01 9 11.01"/></svg></span></div>
        <h3 style="font-size:18px;font-weight:800;margin:0 0 8px;">Your schedule is the schedule</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#4A5560;margin:0;">A reroof can't move until the panels do. We show up when we say we will, on the detach and on the reset, because your whole project is waiting on us.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card" style="padding:30px 28px;">
        <div style="margin-bottom:16px;"><span style="flex-shrink:0;display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;width:48px;height:48px;border-radius:50%;background:#FBF2DF;"><svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#8F5D0C" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 11.08V12a10 10 0 1 1-5.93-9.14"/><polyline points="22 4 12 14.01 9 11.01"/></svg></span></div>
        <h3 style="font-size:18px;font-weight:800;margin:0 0 8px;">Careful hands, careful records</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#4A5560;margin:0;">Panels, rails, and wiring get labeled, photographed, and stored properly. That protects your equipment, and it gives your adjuster clean documentation if there's a claim involved.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card" style="padding:30px 28px;">
        <div style="margin-bottom:16px;"><span style="flex-shrink:0;display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;width:48px;height:48px;border-radius:50%;background:#FBF2DF;"><svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#8F5D0C" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 11.08V12a10 10 0 1 1-5.93-9.14"/><polyline points="22 4 12 14.01 9 11.01"/></svg></span></div>
        <h3 style="font-size:18px;font-weight:800;margin:0 0 8px;">Local and accountable</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#4A5560;margin:0;">We live and work in Northern Colorado. If something isn't right after your reset, you call us and we come back. That's how it should work with a local company.</p>
      </div>
</div>
  </div></section>
<section class="section-pad bg-light">
  <div class="container" style="max-width:900px;">
    <div style="text-align:center;max-width:820px;margin:0 auto 48px;">
    <span class="kicker">FAQ</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(28px,3.4vw,40px);margin:0 0 14px;">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
  </div>
    <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:14px;">
      <details class="faq-item" open>
        <summary>Are you connected to my original solar installer?</summary>
        <p>No, we're an independent detach and reset company. That matters because many installers are booked out for weeks on removal work or charge a premium for it. We work on most residential rooftop systems regardless of who installed them, and if we find something we can't service, we'll tell you up front.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Do you work directly with my roofer and my insurance adjuster?</summary>
        <p>Yes, and it usually makes the whole reroof smoother. We coordinate timing with your roofing crew so the panels are off before tear-off day, and we provide the documentation and line items adjusters expect. You can read more about how pricing works on our <a href="/solar-panel-removal-reinstall-cost/">removal and reinstall cost page</a>.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>What if the hail damaged my panels, not just my roof?</summary>
        <p>We inspect every panel during the detach and flag anything that looks compromised, with photos, so damaged equipment can be added to your claim instead of going back on a brand new roof. Our <a href="/solar-hail-damage-greeley/">solar hail damage page</a> covers what we look for and what your options are.</p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
<section style="background:linear-gradient(150deg,#101826 0%,#16202E 55%,#24374B 100%);padding:88px 24px;text-align:center;">
  <div style="max-width:760px;margin:0 auto;">
    <span class="kicker-dark">Get In Touch</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(28px,3.4vw,40px);color:#fff;margin:0 0 14px;">Ready to Get the Panels Off the Roof?</h2>
    <p style="font-size:16px;line-height:1.7;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.7);margin:0 0 32px;">Free written estimates for Greeley and Northern Colorado. Storm-damage calls answered around the clock.</p>
    <div style="display:flex;justify-content:center;gap:16px;flex-wrap:wrap;">
      <a href="tel:+19702863417" class="btn-green">Call (970) 286-3417</a>
      <a href="/#contact" class="btn-outline-white">Get a Free Written Estimate</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

</Layout>
